{"kind":"report","text":"Approved at exact head 038a85bcc39852251b851bdd910605769c76bc8c, and the citation holds. Run 41332615607 succeeded at 1dc134fd in every step, by my read through `gh` and by `remote/run.txt`, and from 1dc134fd to this head only the note and its manifest change. **No desktop AI app has rendered this, and the routing stays a reading.** J2's acceptance stays open, and the next session decides.\n\n**The press path: right.** In `act`, an `absent` from `view_act` goes to `reopen`, then `view_read`, then a notice, then `return`. There is no second `view_act` on that path, and the control `the press repeats` fails a named assertion. A process with no view refuses before any dispatch, because `#instance` throws first. So the press signed nothing, and the words \"nothing was sent\" are true at that point. A failed reopen says \"No act was sent. Ask for a new card\", which is also true and gives the person a step that works.\n\n**The choice: right.** A restart under a card needs the reopen path in any case, and the other two ways add a store of repository text or a socket with an election, for a smaller remainder.\n\n**Your item 3, pressed: the second act is refused for a change card, though not always by its revision, and that guard does not reach every act.** Two presses take two random keys, so they are two identities, and the per-identity lock file does not stop them. `#refuseWhileOpen` reads the disk with no lock around the send, so both can pass in that moment, as you say. The last guard is the scope. I read the Change card's two acts. A `review-verdict` opens a new `review` item, so it moves no revision that the second press names. The guard `verdict-exists` refuses the second, because it finds a submitted review by that signer on that manifest. A `merge` meets `merge-in-progress`. So the note's \"the scope refuses the second act by its revision\" names the wrong guard for a verdict, and the result stands there. Please correct that sentence at the next edit, to say \"by its revision or its guards\". I did not read each declared card's acts, so this reaches them only as far as a declared act binds its item. An act with no item and no such guard, such as a comment, signs `expected: {}` and would land twice. No card offers one today, so I would not hold this head. If a card ever does, this guard is not there. As you say, these tests use a stand-in that judges nothing, so no run here shows the refusal.\n\nThe window itself is small. It needs a press and a second actor in one moment. A person's card reaches one process, so the second is likely to be the model's process, which holds a different view.\n\n**`cardFor`: right.** The replacement uses a function, it escapes the screen name, and the digest covers the changed bytes. The test holds a declared resource's own screen. `generation` changes for a declared package, which your note states.\n\n**Limits.**\n- A host that sends each call to a different process signs another `read-token` for each press on a new process. It is a permanent act with no other effect, and it costs an entry each time. The logs show one connection, so this waits.\n- The older card's `#current`, and a declared screen's memory of a lost reply, both end in a refusal or a missing button and no second act. The model's `settle` still reads the record. Agreed as limits.\n- A model's input act can answer \"The selected item or revision changed.\" That is safe, because it signs nothing. It will read as a fault to a person, so the grow room's fix after J2 is right.\n\n**One thing to keep an eye on.** Your note says that an earlier chained run of `declared-views-browser.mjs` ended with a Node crash line and no captured reason, and that one later run passed. A pass does not explain a crash. 988ae872 covers the browser scripts, so please name it there if it comes back.\n\n**Evidence.** `SHA256SUMS` is 8a5312ef…, every digest verifies, and no file is writable. The gate's `head.txt` is 1dc134fd, exit 0, with 3537 and 1022 tests. I ran `apps/views/test/two-process.test.mjs` (3 pass), `view-resources.test.ts` and `view-sessions.test.ts` (18 passed), `security-entry-points` (10 pass), check-notes (0 warnings), check-doc-links (1002, 0 broken) and check-commit-messages (3, 0 flagged). The worktree is clean. I did not rerun the controls, the browser script or the deployed witness. The witness signed one `read-token` act on the J2 room, as the note labels.\n\n**Architecture.** No new route, argument or store. The opening tools were already visible to `app`.\n\n**Security.** The opening call reads and signs nothing beyond what the model's call did. The card keeps that call in memory only. No authority changes, and the rule that a press is never repeated is held by a named control.\n\n**Simplification.** `isAbsent` and `reopen` serve both paths. Nothing to remove.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:29a864b501c45b2c6d9f87989bf7fe232ff065a9","binding":"assigned","head":"038a85bcc39852251b851bdd910605769c76bc8c","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3fb12658f93c4671740712d365f28e6039ba6e57\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:12f75101d0fc9494769afa3c7ca88dec4742146f\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3fb12658f93c4671740712d365f28e6039ba6e57","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}